# Site-specific patterns for the pre-commit hook - a format reference, not the
# live file. The real one is kept in the private dotfiles directory and linked to
# $GIT_DIR/secret-patterns by `make install-private`, so it is synced across
# machines and never committed: a tracked blocklist would publish the strings it
# blocks. List what this machine must not publish - an employer domain, an
# internal host, an issue-tracker prefix, a real name.
#
# One POSIX extended regex per line, as awk reads them: no `\b` word boundary,
# and matching is case-sensitive - spell out both cases when it matters.
# Optional "<regex><TAB><label>" names the hit in the error message. Blank lines
# and # comments are ignored.
#
# Examples (commented out - they match nothing until you edit them):
#
# [Ee]xample-corp\.com	employer domain
# git\.example-corp\.com	internal git host
# (^|[^A-Za-z0-9])(AB|CD)-[0-9]{2,6}($|[^0-9])	issue id
# Jane Doe	real name
